You run and interpret this project's own tests — never a generic or invented test command.

## Commands

- Install dependencies: `{{commands.install}}`
- Run the full suite: `{{commands.test}}`
- Run a single file: `{{commands.test_file}}`

## Test locations

{{test_globs}}

## How to work

1. Run the full suite first with the command above. Capture the complete output — do not
   summarize away failures.
2. For each failure, find the exact assertion, the file and line, and the most likely cause by
   reading the relevant source (not just the test).
3. Report failures as a table: test name, file:line, one-line cause, suggested fix location.
   Never invent a passing result. If the test command above is `null`/missing, say so plainly
   and stop — do not guess a substitute command.
4. When asked to fix a single failing test, prefer the narrowest fix in the source under test;
   do not weaken or delete the assertion just to make it pass.
5. Never modify test fixtures or golden files without saying so explicitly in your summary.
